    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class (the other two are a base class and a helper). The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` field so that creating an owner records how many existing owners already shared the same first and last name (case-insensitively) at create time, and the value is returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges, each in the layer where it belongs:\n\n- **`Owner` model** (`model/Owner.java`): added a persisted `namesakeCount` (`Integer`, column `namesake_count`) with getter/setter, mirroring the existing `customerCode`/`householdId` derived fields.\n- **Service** (`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`): in `saveOwner`, when the owner is new, stamp `namesakeCount` via a new small private helper `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)`. The helper reuses the existing `OwnerRepository.findByLastNameIgnoreCase(...)` and filters by `firstName.equalsIgnoreCase(...)` \u2014 the same reuse pattern `householdMembers` already follows. Because the owner isn't persisted yet, the count naturally reflects only owners existing *before* this create.\n- **OpenAPI spec** (`resources/openapi.yml`): added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field; MapStruct maps it automatically by name (no mapper change needed).\n- **Schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`): added the `namesake_count INTEGER` column so every profile's `owners` table carries it.\n\nThe `coreCountsNamesakes` acceptance test and the full suite build green.",
